      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Successful use of nonnarcotic, thoracic epidural analgesia for the control of pain associated with pleural sclerosis was accomplished in three gynecologic oncology patients with severe respiratory compromise due to malignant pleural effusions. Excellent analgesia was obtained with no observed anesthetic complications."},
